nodecode-makernice is a rewrite of makernice's makernice/makernice-plugin:

  https://github.com/makernice/makernice-plugin
  commit ebdff055312c9e19f27caa0fe108661d64e74643
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Makernice Team (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original is configuration only -- a plugin.json, an
mcp.json naming the remote MCP server at mcp.makernice.com, and four skills
(makernice-setup, product-video, trend-remix, cost-planner). Everything the
user gets from it is served by that server, so the cell is its client in
Common Lisp: it speaks MCP's streamable-HTTP protocol (initialize,
notifications/initialized, tools/call, the Mcp-Session-Id header, a JSON or
event-stream answer) to the same url, and registers the server's eight tools
under the same names with a makernice_ prefix -- list_models, estimate_cost,
generate, check_job, cancel_job, list_trends, get_balance, get_topup_link --
with the descriptions and the input parameters the plugin's evals pin. The one
flow all four skills teach is kept as the primer behind (help :makernice) and
made a local rule where a local rule is possible: generate refuses without the
price the user approved (max_cost_usd, the amount_usd estimate_cost answered)
and without a stable request_id, so a retry is never charged twice; a forgotten
session (HTTP 404) re-runs the handshake once; a refused token names where the
token came from, never the token.

What was left out, and why: the OAuth sign-in itself. The original left it to
whichever client installed the plugin (Claude Code's /mcp, Hermes's
auth: oauth, Cursor, Gemini CLI), and the cell takes the bearer it issues in
its section or the environment instead of running a browser flow of its own --
so the sign-in is one step the user does once in a client that has one. The
skills' four documents are one primer rather than four files, because a cell's
manual is one text read with every request. The per-client install
instructions in the README (Claude Code's plugin marketplace, Cursor's folder,
Gemini CLI, LobeHub, `npx skills add`) are not repeated: the cell is the
client. LICENSE is the original repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
